# `!`-move of a collection with a LIVE element borrow, move-BIND shape.
# `String first = v.get(0).unwrap()` binds a deferred CollectionRef into
# v's buffer; `Vector[String] w = !v` must sever it (materialize `first`)
# BEFORE the transfer — the Expr::Move lowering used to call
# cow_before_mutation only for bare params, so mutating `w` read-through
# corrupted `first` (printed "gamma" instead of "alpha").
# NOTE: the bind MUST be the `.get(i).unwrap()` shape — `v[i]` binds take a
# different, already-safe path and would guard nothing.
void main():
    Vector[String] v = ["alpha", "beta"]
    String first = v.get(0).unwrap()
    Vector[String] w = !v
    w.set(0, "gamma")
    print(first)
    print(w.get(0).unwrap())
